// GRIM WORLD: sampled sound effects.
//
// Every other sound in this game is synthesised at runtime and costs nothing to
// download. These four are not, and the reason is narrow: an anvil strike and a
// campfire bed are the two things oscillators are worst at. Metal wants six
// inharmonic partials that all decay at different rates, and a fire wants
// broadband noise that never repeats. Synthesis gets close enough to notice
// that it is close enough.
//
// Generated once with ElevenLabs text-to-sound-effects (harness/sfx.py), then
// trimmed to where each sound actually stops and encoded at a bitrate matched
// to the content: 96k for the tonal metal, 64k for the broadband fire. Base64
// costs a third on top of the mp3, and that is already counted in the numbers
// below. Total added to the bundle: 221 KB.
//
// fire-bed is a TRUE LOOP. ElevenLabs' v2 model takes loop:true and the join
// was measured at a discontinuity of 0.003 against a natural sample-to-sample
// variation of 0.24 inside the clip, roughly a hundred times smaller than the
// audio's own texture, so the wrap cannot be heard. Do not re-encode it with a
// tool that trims silence: that is what would break the seam.

