  // -- spells and arrow impacts (patch 55.283) ------------------------------------
  // Kevin: "some of the sounds for magic actually still sound like sword swings
  // and sword hits". They did. Fire landing played the sword crit, an arrow
  // landing played the sword hit, and casting heal played the item pickup
  // chime. None of these were spell sounds at all, they were the melee voice
  // reused because nothing else was wired.
  //
  // ARROWS are deliberately restrained. Kevin asked for a soft dull thud on
  // flesh, not gore, and the flesh take was chosen on measurement: spectral
  // centroid 205 Hz with 95 percent of its energy under 400 Hz, which is the
  // dullest of the batch. The armour take is the opposite by design, centroid
  // 4920 Hz, because an arrow off steel is a bright ricochet.
  //
  // FIRE has a crackle layer mixed in from the campfire bed, high passed at
  // 1500 Hz. The generated fire takes measured almost no energy above 3 kHz,
  // which is why they read as a whoosh rather than a fire.
  //
  // FROST IMPACT was chosen on peak position: 0.03, meaning it peaks at its
  // very start. The alternatives peaked at the END, which is the wrong shape
  // for an impact and reads as a rewind.

